id: ignited
name: Ignited
kind: conditions
# One stack per clock, so the Square stays Aflame until the last attacker's clock runs out
# rather than the first. The cap only has to be out of anybody's reach: a Square is Aflame
# or it is not, and every stack past the first changes nothing but how long.
maxStacks: 99
# Not a Combat Condition: the entry makes a Square Aflame and never names one.
combatCondition: no
# The Environmental Quality this mark puts on the Square while it is held. Named here and
# not in the code, where no Quality is named.
quality: aflame
source: Core Rule
description: >
  The ground under you is on fire. Your Square is Aflame.
text: >
  Ignited: the Elemental (Fire) Profile's mark. "Any Squares occupied by Character(s) who
  take Damage from this Attacking Maneuver become Aflame (see — Environmental Qualities,
  Battle Environments) until the start of your next turn."

---

# --- The name is this system's ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The entry makes a Square Aflame, and this system has no Squares. Environmental Qualities
# are on the character, ticked on the Battlefields tab, so the fire lands on the character
# whose Square it was - the one who took the Damage.
#
# A mark rather than a tick in that list for the reason Darkened is one: it runs out on the
# attacker's clock ("until the start of YOUR next turn"), and a tick the effect had added
# would have to be taken away again past whatever the player ticked in the meantime. So the
# list stays the player's and `qualitiesOf` adds the Quality in the `quality:` header while
# this is held.
#
# No effects of its own. What burning ground does is the Aflame Quality's file, and this
# only decides that the file is read.
